{"id": "EUVD-2026-81883", "enisaUuid": "4956d4a9-7d7a-3c35-87f6-9470a2e9d905", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\narm64: hibernate: Restore DAIF state on error\n\nSashiko AI has reported that if swsusp_mte_save_tags() for some reason\nfails we return from swsusp_arch_suspend() with DAIF being masked -\nthat is not what we'd expect. Restore the saved DAIF state before\nreturning from the error path.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:08:18", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:01:08", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f5693dfaf28d66e7e880feafd1778d3715869efc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2c941f383a53e188cd6fe3a129eb9b52b298e683", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cb51a05498e755d900900ff4b8503b4da4325996", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ad3839fe2114bb092846df79edd8d119e148b8c3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c8c6835f62a7f9fc68865e85397d13a2dc9210fb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/519e7de2c4c7b92ef57d4404b7e564aa9be24143", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/77053624d03359a4e2ec47d7106639ec9a498c2b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/541549827889d0380fd73f8aacb5de6ef7a5a1ac"], "aliases": ["GHSA-49wg-x228-h4jh", "CVE-2026-90290"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "03bef7f2-f9ec-3b91-a589-e88a947df2ed", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "0a718004-e84d-3048-910f-7c1adbd1685d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.221"}, {"id": "16f73aeb-cac5-3011-ba87-72876035448f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "26cef75e-2cfe-36d1-ac8c-80925da0d7ae", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "286ba2ce-9a64-3812-aa20-c7438a1c81df", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.10"}, {"id": "4daf1